Scenario: Social Media Footer Navigation
	End users should be able to view all links in the social media section of the footer.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the footer "Facebook" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay - Home | Facebook"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay - Home | Facebook"
	And I click on the footer "Github" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay Inc. · GitHub"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay Inc. · GitHub"
	And I click on the footer "Instagram" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay, Inc. (@liferayinc) • Instagram photos and videos"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay, Inc. (@liferayinc) • Instagram photos and videos"
	And I click on the footer "LinkedIn" social media link
	And I select the pop up window
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the pop up window
	And I click on the footer "Twitter" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay (@Liferay) / Twitter"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay (@Liferay) / Twitter"
	And I click on the footer "YouTube" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay - YouTube"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And I close the window titled "Liferay - YouTube"

