Scenario: View homepage title and meta description
	The homepage title and meta description should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the current page title should be "Digital Experience Software Tailored to Your Needs | Liferay"
	And the current page meta description should be "Build portals, intranets, websites and connected experiences on the most extensible digital experience platform around. Learn more."

Scenario: View OG Tags
	The homepage og tags should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the current page og title tag should be "Digital Experience Software Tailored to Your Needs | Liferay"
	And the current page og description tag should be "Build portals, intranets, websites and connected experiences on the most extensible digital experience platform around. Learn more."
	And the current page og url tag should be "https://www-uat.liferay.com/"
	And the current page og image tag should be "https://www-uat.liferay.com/documents/10182/0/open_graph_image+%281%29.png/a608e357-83f6-e392-979c-6599a8618634/open_graph_image+%281%29.png?version=1.0&t=1646949040894&imagePreview=1"

Scenario: View homepage hreflang tags
	All hreflang tags on the homepage should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the hreflang tag for the relative language url "zh/" should be "zh"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "es/" should be "es"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "en-AU/" should be "en-AU"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "ja/" should be "ja"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "it/" should be "it"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "fr/" should be "fr"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "" should be "en"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "pt/" should be "pt"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "de/" should be "de"

Scenario: View homepage hreflang canonical tags
	Correct hreflang canonical tags should be present upon language changes.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Chinese"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "zh" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Australian English"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "en-AU" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "American English"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "en" should be present
	When I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "French"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "fr" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "German"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "de" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Italian"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "it" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Portuguese"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "pt" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Spanish"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "es" should be present

Scenario: View all homepage links
    End users should be able to view all links in the homepage.

    Given I go to the www homepage
    And I click on the "Learn More" link under the "Introducing Liferay Experience Cloud" section on the homepage
    Then there should be no errors on the page
    And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com/products/liferay-experience-cloud"
    When I go to the www homepage
    And I click on the "Personalize Your Digital Experiences" link under the "Engage Your Audience with Personalized Digital Experiences" section on the homepage 
    Then there should be no errors on the page
    And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com/products/dxp/engage"
    When I go to the www homepage
    And I click on the "Empower Your Users" link under the "Support and Empower Your Users with Self-Service" section on the homepage
    Then there should be no errors on the page
    And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com/products/dxp/support"
    When I go to the www homepage
    And I click on the "Connect Your Revenue" link under the "Grow Revenue with a Seamless B2B Commerce Experience" section on the homepage
    Then there should be no errors on the page
    And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com/products/dxp/transact"

Scenario: View all homepage sections illustration
    End users should be able to view all sections illustration in the homepage.

    Given I go to the www homepage
    Then I should be able to view the illustration for the "Introducing Liferay Experience Cloud" section on the homepage
    And I should be able to view the illustration for the "Engage Your Audience with Personalized Digital Experiences" section on the homepage
    And I should be able to view the illustration for the "Support and Empower Your Users with Self-Service" section on the homepage
    And I should be able to view the illustration for the "Grow Revenue with a Seamless B2B Commerce Experience" section on the homepage